  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2026 Morocco Earthquake project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Activities take place in the provinces of Azilal, Chichaoua, Taroudant, El Haouz, and Marrakesh in Morocco.
Implementation is concentrated at community level in Taroudant and with LWUAs across all four provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct support targets 22,005 people, including 21,955 community members and 50 MRC staff and volunteers.
Indirectly, 18,032 people will benefit through improved water management, DRR systems, and strengthened MRC capacity.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It is a 14 month DRR and WASH programme supporting eVCA based community action plans, LWUA technical training, and national WASH preparedness.
Activities include implementing PoAs in 39 douars, training 8 LWUA groups, and building WASH contingency stock for 15,000 people.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen climate smart community resilience after the 2023 El Haouz earthquake.
It addresses major gaps in DRR knowledge, preparedness, and WASH systems that continue to expose communities to high risk.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is implemented through community led eVCA action plans, financial disbursements to trained local associations, and continuous technical support from MRC and IFRC teams.
It also delivers LWUA technical trainings, strengthens national WASH in emergency capacity through equipment and SOPs, and ensures quality via M&amp;E systems, CEA, PGI and safeguarding mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
